        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c838224a-35b9-5efe-96c3-0b32d4eaf3fc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Nol Card, Octopus card, Oyster Card, Upass\n- Places: Dubai, Hong Kong, London\n- Concepts: electronic ticketing, contactless stored-value smart cards, public transport payments\n\nFacts:\n- The Octopus card was launched in Hong Kong in September 1997 to collect fares for the territory's mass transit system.\n- The Octopus card system was the second contactless smart card system in the world after the Korean Upass.\n- The Octopus card later became a widely used payment system for all public transport in Hong Kong and contributed to the development of London's Oyster Card.\n- The Nol Card is an electronic ticketing card for all modes of public transport in Dubai and was released in August 2009.\n- The Octopus card is a reusable contactless stored-value smart card used for electronic payments in both online and offline systems in Hong Kong.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
